From aefdb15d4a2757aabffd2d36bf3b3314c3e94f3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:24:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the EDID of a connector as the connector has
 it now

CDRMConnector::GetEDID() took the id of the EDID blob from the values read
with the connector, and only the connector that Kodi moves to is read again
(CDRMConnector::Refresh()). A driver puts a new blob in the EDID property at
each probe of a connector (drm_edid_connector_update() replaces it), and DRM
gives the id of a blob that was let go to the next blob it makes (idr_alloc()
of drm_mode_object.c, the lowest free id): an id kept from before then names
the EDID of another display. With an LG C5 on HDMI-A-3, a Samsung Odyssey
G60SD on HDMI-A-2 and an LG UltraGear on DP-2 of an RTX 4080 SUPER, the
choice of the outputs kept on for the sound named HDMI-A-2 "LG TV SSCR2",
DP-2 "LG TV SSCR2" or "not known" and HDMI-A-3 "LG ULTRAGEAR" in turn, while
the kernel and the EDIDs read from sysfs said otherwise: the sound of the TV
was taken for the monitor's, the monitor was lit again "for the sound in use"
at the next change of mode (the notification "The sound of ... comes back"),
and its ELD coming back sent the sound to it for a few seconds.

GetEDID() now reads the property's value as it is now, takes its blob, and
reads the value again: the EDID is taken only when the id held, else read
again (three times at most). Where the property cannot be read, the value
read with the connector, as before. Every user of GetEDID() gets the EDID
of the connector's own display: the outputs kept for the sound, the name a
display is shown by, the Dolby Vision of the other outputs, the notification.

Compiled with the compile command of the build (an injected error fails
there). Not run on a GPU: what tells it is the line of the log that lists
"the outputs that could carry it", each connector with its own display.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp | 53 ++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
index d4027d3..fcfebb6 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMConnector.cpp
@@ -155,24 +155,41 @@ std::string CDRMConnector::GetName()
 
 std::vector<uint8_t> CDRMConnector::GetEDID() const
 {
-
-  uint64_t blob_id = GetPropertyValue("EDID").value_or(0);
-
-  if (blob_id == 0)
+  // Hades: the EDID property as the connector has it now, not the value read with the connector:
+  // a driver puts a new blob there at each probe of a connector (drm_edid_connector_update()
+  // replaces the blob), and DRM gives the id of a blob let go to the next blob it makes
+  // (idr_alloc(), the lowest free id), so an id kept from before can name the EDID of another
+  // display (with three displays on an NVIDIA card, each connector was told the display of
+  // another). The id is read again after its blob, and the blob is taken only when the id held.
+  // Where the property cannot be read now, the value read with the connector, as before.
+  for (int attempt = 0; attempt < 3; ++attempt)
   {
-    CLog::LogF(LOGDEBUG, "failed to find EDID property for connector: {}",
-               m_connector->connector_id);
-    return {};
+    const std::optional<uint64_t> now = ReadPropertyValue("EDID");
+    const uint64_t blob_id = now ? *now : GetPropertyValue("EDID").value_or(0);
+
+    if (blob_id == 0)
+    {
+      CLog::LogF(LOGDEBUG, "failed to find EDID property for connector: {}",
+                 m_connector->connector_id);
+      return {};
+    }
+
+    drmModePropertyBlobPtr blob = drmModeGetPropertyBlob(m_fd, blob_id);
+    if (!blob)
+    {
+      if (now)
+        continue; // (let go in between: the property has another blob now)
+      return {};
+    }
+
+    auto data = static_cast<uint8_t*>(blob->data);
+    auto edid = std::vector<uint8_t>(data, data + blob->length);
+
+    drmModeFreePropertyBlob(blob);
+
+    if (now && ReadPropertyValue("EDID") != now)
+      continue; // (replaced while it was read: the id may have named another blob by then)
+    return edid;
   }
-
-  drmModePropertyBlobPtr blob = drmModeGetPropertyBlob(m_fd, blob_id);
-  if (!blob)
-    return {};
-
-  auto data = static_cast<uint8_t*>(blob->data);
-  auto edid = std::vector<uint8_t>(data, data + blob->length);
-
-  drmModeFreePropertyBlob(blob);
-
-  return edid;
+  return {};
 }
